  "result": "I found the bug in `Cart.remove` and fixed it. The method compared each line's item **name** to the SKU you passed in (`l.item.name != sku` in `shop/models.py:33`). `'sku-1'` never equals `'Widget'`, so nothing was ever removed. The method now compares by SKU (`l.item.sku != sku`), which matches how `Cart.add` finds existing lines.\n\nChecks:\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1` (only the Gadget is left). Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest discover`, and all 6 passed. None of them call `Cart.remove`, though, so the passing tests don't confirm this fix; only the demo run does. I can add a regression test if you want one.",
